WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.435
-Our next guests are
the creators and stars

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:04.203
of the show "Three Busy Debras,"

00:00:04.203 --> 00:00:05.805
which is streaming now
on HBO Max.

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:07.306
Let's take a look.

00:00:07.306 --> 00:00:09.509
-I'll hack into the mainframe
using top-of-the-line software.

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:12.711
And one fun fact about me is,
there's nothing fun about me.

00:00:12.711 --> 00:00:14.247
-I'll be
the Debra on the ground,

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:19.185
and a fun fact about me is,
my favorite food is...

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:21.587
-I'm young for my grade
because I have a late birthday,

00:00:21.587 --> 00:00:23.422
and I'm gonna distract
the security guard

00:00:23.422 --> 00:00:25.558
doing what I do best.

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:29.695
♪♪

00:00:29.695 --> 00:00:31.731
[ Laughter ]
-Please welcome to the show

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:35.735
Sandy Honig, Mitra Jouhari,
and Alyssa Stonoha.

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:37.803
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:37.803 --> 00:00:40.907
[ Mid-tempo music plays ]

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:50.717
♪♪

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:54.720
Well, I am so, so happy

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:57.657
to have all three of you here.
-We are so excited to be here.

00:00:57.657 --> 00:00:58.924
-Please do not
take this personally.

00:00:58.924 --> 00:01:01.194
Mitra, I'm a little extra happy
to have you here,

00:01:01.194 --> 00:01:03.396
because Mitra --
this is a true story --

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:07.433 line:0%
you are a former intern at
"Late Night With Seth Meyers."

00:01:07.433 --> 00:01:08.968 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:13.572 line:0%
You are our first -- our first
returning intern,

00:01:13.572 --> 00:01:16.008
and you probably don't
remember your last day.

00:01:16.008 --> 00:01:17.977
Remember, you said to me,
like, "I'll be back!"

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:20.612
-Yeah, yeah, it was nasty,
but you deserved it.

00:01:20.612 --> 00:01:22.815
You said a lot of really mean
stuff before I said that.

00:01:22.815 --> 00:01:25.184
-I did but that's -- I try to
drive people to succeed.

00:01:25.184 --> 00:01:27.086
Did you have a nice time
as an intern here?

00:01:27.086 --> 00:01:28.587
-I had a really nice time.
-Good.

00:01:28.587 --> 00:01:31.157
I mean, we can't believe.
We're so happy to have you back.

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:34.160
And it is so lovely to have
all of you guys together.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:37.329
You met around the same time,
you were saying.

00:01:37.329 --> 00:01:39.465
I guess, around seven times
ago -- seven years ago.

00:01:39.465 --> 00:01:42.101
But this is -- these are
characters you created

00:01:42.101 --> 00:01:44.170
the first time you did
an improv scene together?

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:48.308
-Yes, we were all, like --
We sort of

00:01:48.308 --> 00:01:50.310
vaguely knew each other
through mutual friends,

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:52.679
and everyone kept telling us
we should hang out.

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:55.314
And so we got together and
we did an improv set.

00:01:55.314 --> 00:01:58.250
And ahead of hanging out,
we were all, like,

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:01.253
just having a hard time
finding a time.

00:02:01.253 --> 00:02:02.655
We were all just too busy.

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:05.524
So when we got onstage, we
ended up doing this improv set

00:02:05.524 --> 00:02:08.160
where we accidentally
named all of ourselves Debra.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:11.130
And the whole thing was just
about like, "We're so busy.

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:14.300
We couldn't possibly make time
for each other."

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:16.469
And then that was how we came up
with the idea for a show.

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:17.737
-And we haven't
had an idea since.

00:02:17.737 --> 00:02:19.038
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:21.507
-That's what the remarkable
thing about you guys is.

00:02:21.507 --> 00:02:24.544
Your first idea was a good one
and your last one.

00:02:24.544 --> 00:02:25.912
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.912 --> 00:02:29.014
You did have a premiere,
but you had COVID, Mitra,

00:02:29.014 --> 00:02:30.616
so you could not go.
-Yes, on purpose.

00:02:30.616 --> 00:02:31.750
-[ Laughing ] COVID on purpose.

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:33.586
You guys came up with
a very novel way

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:35.688
to make sure that Mitra was
with you at the premiere.

00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:37.022
What did you come up with?

00:02:37.022 --> 00:02:39.826
-You know, we thought

00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:42.494
the only way that we
could honor her spirit

00:02:42.494 --> 00:02:45.965
is to tape a picture of
her face onto a sex doll.

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:47.366
-Yeah.

00:02:47.366 --> 00:02:49.202
-And toss her
around the party.

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:53.106
-You know, I thought it
would look a little slapdash,

00:02:53.106 --> 00:02:55.575
but you obviously got
some real professionals,

00:02:55.575 --> 00:02:57.310
because you can hardly tell.

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:59.212
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.212 --> 00:03:02.481
-And you know, it's hard
to tell in the photo,

00:03:02.481 --> 00:03:05.318
but the sex doll actually does
have three tempting holes.

00:03:05.318 --> 00:03:06.552
-Oh, wow.

00:03:06.552 --> 00:03:09.555
If I find out
you have a hashtag ad...

00:03:09.555 --> 00:03:11.791
[ Laughter ]
You guys also --

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:14.193
Here's your executive producer,
Amy Poehler.

00:03:14.193 --> 00:03:18.464
-The way we got introduced
to working with her was,

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:21.434
we had been doing our play,
"Three Busy Debras,"

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:25.671
in a black-box theater.
And then we decided

00:03:25.671 --> 00:03:28.774
we wanted to put on the show
again, but it was --

00:03:28.774 --> 00:03:31.243
-No one would have us.
-No one would have us,

00:03:31.243 --> 00:03:32.979
basically, 'cause
the show was disgusting.

00:03:32.979 --> 00:03:34.980
And then --
-So, wait,

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:36.815
this is no black-box theater
would have you?

00:03:36.815 --> 00:03:39.052
-Yeah, we couldn't find
a single place in New York.

00:03:39.052 --> 00:03:42.322
-Well, there aren't a ton of
theaters here.

00:03:42.322 --> 00:03:44.623
-We used to do this show
at this black-box theater

00:03:44.623 --> 00:03:46.159
in Brooklyn
called The Annoyance,

00:03:46.159 --> 00:03:49.161
and we made such a disgusting
mess every week.

00:03:49.161 --> 00:03:52.564
We would boil hard-boiled eggs
and peel them onstage

00:03:52.564 --> 00:03:55.468
at the beginning of the show.
It created quite a stink.

00:03:55.468 --> 00:03:59.271
There was actually
a mystery smell in the theater,

00:03:59.271 --> 00:04:00.806
and we were, like,
the number-one people

00:04:00.806 --> 00:04:02.909
being like, "Ew,
this theater, like, stinks.

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:04.777
Like, why does it smell so bad?"

00:04:04.777 --> 00:04:08.448
Until we received an e-mail
that it was, in fact, us,

00:04:08.448 --> 00:04:12.318
and our props that had
rotting eggshells in them.

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:15.121
-And then we decided that we --
that you --

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:18.457
We wanted to perform
at Carnegie Hall as a joke.

00:04:18.457 --> 00:04:21.794
We were like, "It'd be so funny
do this show at Carnegie Hall.

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:23.596
I wonder what that's like.
I wonder how hard that is."

00:04:23.596 --> 00:04:25.164
And it turns out,
you just have to pay for it.

00:04:25.164 --> 00:04:26.732
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.732 --> 00:04:28.668
Everyone who performs there
is just renting it.

00:04:28.668 --> 00:04:32.472
So we did a Kickstarter
to rent it,

00:04:32.472 --> 00:04:37.209
but the tiers
to get lights and tech

00:04:37.209 --> 00:04:40.346
were a lot more expensive
than the basic package

00:04:40.346 --> 00:04:42.548
of getting onstage.
-Yeah.

00:04:42.548 --> 00:04:46.519
So, we did perform
an original two-act musical,

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:49.188
um, about the
three busy Debras,

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:51.190
to an audience
with the house lights up.

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:53.059
We could see
everyone's eyes and faces.

00:04:53.059 --> 00:04:56.061
And five minutes
before the play started,

00:04:56.061 --> 00:04:58.163
Amy e-mailed us,
wishing us good luck.

00:04:58.163 --> 00:04:59.365
-Sandy, famously,
was checking e-mail

00:04:59.365 --> 00:05:00.966
before the biggest night
of our lives.

00:05:00.966 --> 00:05:04.437
-And I can't explain that one.

00:05:04.437 --> 00:05:06.839
I don't know why, right before,
I was like, "Oh,

00:05:06.839 --> 00:05:10.008
let me check my e-mail.
That's a great idea."

00:05:10.008 --> 00:05:11.910
-And thank God you did.
-And thank God I did.

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:14.380 line:0%
-You guys also have a lot of
original music in the show,

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:15.714 line:0%
and you have an soundtrack
coming out.

00:05:15.714 --> 00:05:17.549 line:0%
That's really exciting.
When can we hear this?

00:05:17.549 --> 00:05:19.418 line:0%
-June 24th.
-Alright!

00:05:19.418 --> 00:05:22.488
June 24th, the music of
"Three Busy Debras"!

00:05:22.488 --> 00:05:25.458
You guys, thank you so much
for being here.

00:05:25.458 --> 00:05:27.860
It's lovely to meet you both.
It's lovely to have you back.

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:31.998
Sandy Honig, Mitra Jouhari,
Alyssa Stonoha.

00:05:31.998 --> 00:05:34.099
All episodes of
"Three Busy Debras"

00:05:34.099 --> 00:05:35.434
are streaming on HBO Max.

00:05:35.434 --> 00:05:36.769
And the show's
original soundtrack

00:05:36.769 --> 00:05:38.905
will be available to stream.
We'll be right back.

